Iconic now, but really only because of Smash Brothers.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.420
Again, yeah. You know, like, Smash Brothers, yeah, like, well, Duck Hunt, we kind of, we landed on the side that that was an iconic game still.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:18.480
Joe, for sure, that was a game of, 2018 game of the year.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.600
I think Joe's still playing it.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.120
I'm down to talk about Duck Hunt again this episode.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:22.980
Fantastic.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.780
And welcoming back Sam here for a minute.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.960
Hey. And that was it.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.340
That was us welcoming back Sam.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.540
Now I'm back. But I do kind of want to get into Ice Climber real fast before we go into first impressions.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.060
This is a Nintendo R&D 1 game.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.620
They're responsible for most of the NES launch games.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.800
It launched, and it was a big deal then, and it came out a couple different iterations and ports.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:48.040
It was part of the NES Classic series on Game Boy Advance and made its way into NES Remix.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:54.560
But I don't think any of this would have happened if, like, Smash Brothers didn't introduce Nana and Popo again.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.500
It's kind of, well, I guess let's talk about that.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.200
Let's get our first impressions.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.400
Sean, you want to lead us through?

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:26.340
Well, going back to just my conscious, like, understanding of it before Smash, I didn't know it existed.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.960
I didn't. And when, like, they were announced for the game, I'm like, I don't know who they are.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.560
And when you say the game, which Smash Brothers iteration are you referring to?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.120
Melee. Okay, yeah, yeah.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.300
Because I think that is, like, the big surprise.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.200
And it's kind of like that for so many entries in Melee, too.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.860
Roy is another one I think about where it's like...

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.100
Well, Roy, he debuted in Melee, right?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.980
Yeah, and it's like, what is this character?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.940
I mean, like, you might have seen Marth in an issue of Nintendo Power or something.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.660
But Roy was a reveal, and Fire Emblem as a series was never given any love outside there.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.960
But that's a whole other story.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.660
Unfortunately, we might never talk about a Fire Emblem game on this because...

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.340
No, we can't just go until we're 40 years old, man.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.120
The NES games were Japanese only.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.960
No, no, Fire Emblem is an NES series.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.420
I did not know. Yeah, very cool.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.900
But, okay, so let's get into first impressions again.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:18.800
Okay, my first impression of Ice Climber is this is, like, the whole, like, jump aspect.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.960
It's a very jump-first game.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.560
It's like proto-Mario, but...

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.340
So you had a platformer vibe at all, or...?

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.620
It felt platformy.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.620
Okay, yeah. I mean, it's definitely, you're jumping on platforms in this game.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.140
I hated the game.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.920
Okay. I did not like...

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:35.760
As a first impression.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:36.660
That's my first impression.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.700
Okay. Yeah, I was...

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.820
I mean, even before first impressions, I mean, I love Smash Bros, and so I was really excited

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:48.260
to see where the Ice Climbers came from, and it was just not fun.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.480
It felt like it was...

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.120
Like, when I first got it and I beat the first level, I was thinking, is this...

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.020
This is it? You just jump a little bit, and then you get to the top, and then...

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.720
The concept doesn't really evolve.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.160
Yeah. And that's it.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.520
And it's just harder to jump sometimes, and there's moving platforms, but you're still just

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.820
jumping up, and it's just...

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.240
I don't know. I was really disappointed just off the bat.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.760
And, like, if the game is all about jumping, the jumping feels terrible.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.420
Yeah. Yeah, it's not a good jump.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.420
Joe? So, I mean, I was kind of on the...

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.340
In between with it.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.740
I thought it was moderately fun.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.620
I didn't think there was anything that made it great, but I didn't think there was anything

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.020
that made it terrible either, so I think I'm the only one who didn't...

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.720
Well, unless you have a different opinion, Mike.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.740
It was okay. The jumping was definitely one of my first things, though.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.560
The jumping does not work very well.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.940
That's the whole game, though.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.020
Yeah, I agree. No, I agree.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.640
But it wasn't game-breaking for me.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.280
It got annoying every once in a while.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.820
There'd be a thing where I was like, eh, I should have landed on that.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.660
Right. I just want to chime in with one initial impression that's a little different, is that I thought

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:50.040
the game was fun at first, and that I could get through the clunkiness of the controls.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.660
I felt the controls right away.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.560
I was like, wow, this is unresponsive, and I'm not that fun.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.800
But I thought, okay, the concept's cool enough.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.060
Maybe I can get through it.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.080
And by Mountain 4, that impression...

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.740
That first impression was gone.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.660
And now my real impression of the game had formed.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.140
Yeah. Okay, cool.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.660
So, since we're talking about the game, let's just go really quick into the objective.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.920
Anybody want to give this a stab?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:16.780
You're supposed to climb the ice to the top of the mountain where a, like...

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.940
An aubergine. Is it an aubergine?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.400
Yeah. An eggplant.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.400
An aubergine bird. Oh, the condor.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.740
Okay, a condor.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.060
I thought it was a pterodactyl.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.880
Or a pterodactyl. It looks like an eagle.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.780
That has stolen your eggplant or carrot or what have you.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.300
So, wait, wait. It really is a condor?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:33.400
Yeah. That's perfect.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.300
Wow. Is that a manual thing?

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.240
It was... Sam the manual.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:41.540
I did read the manual for every game that we played.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.000
That's wonderful. So, we're going to have to do a little manual section later.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.240
But continue, Sean.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.620
So, you're climbing the top of the mountain to get this eggplant along the way.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:53.260
Along the way, you break ice blocks with your hammer.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.660
And then there are these things that try to block you.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:04.800
There are many animals or puffy balls or ice particulates that try to stop you on your way.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.740
And, you know, just real fast, talk about enemies.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.300
It kind of bugged me that on the box, there's that polar bear.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:13.520
I never got to that level where the polar bear shows up.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.960
So, can I actually tell you my experience with that polar bear?

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.720
Yes. I had forgotten that it was on the box.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.260
I mean, it's just kind of a background thing on the box.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.400
I just didn't really notice it.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:32.360
And I was playing multiplayer, and we were maybe on Mountain 7 or something.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:37.840
And suddenly, out of nowhere, that polar bear in a Speedo or whatever that thing is comes running out.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.020
It comes running out. I don't think it's a Speedo.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.100
It's faster than anything else.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.560
I don't know what it is.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.180
But it comes running out.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.900
No, it's taller and faster than anything else.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.900
It's kind of frightening.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.300
Were you taking some time? What's that?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.760
I think that the polar bear only comes out if you're, like, taking too long.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.060
Maybe I'm just, like, maybe I'm wrong.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.740
It just came out. We dodged it.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:57.880
And it left.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.060
And it was gone. We never saw it again.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.900
That's like the polar bear is, like, its way of saying, like, hurry up.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.560
Yeah. Like, wow.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.160
No, I don't know. I never saw it.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.400
Yeah. Okay.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.740
Where I wanted to go from there, though, because I don't want to get too far into the game before

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.240
we just start talking about the mountains themselves.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.340
And I feel like the difficulty spikes very quickly in this game.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:21.420
Yeah. To the point where it's super easy to get through mountain one.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.560
Like, there's almost very little obstacle in your way.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.720
You get a taste for the bonus game.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:32.480
And then once you hit, like, mountain four, the platforming in the game is so tough where, like,

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.100
you have to wait for the clouds to line up perfectly.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:38.440
Yeah, that's... And if you miss one jump, you're falling all the way down.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:42.760
There's a lot of precision jumping, and they don't really give you the tools to effectively do it.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:49.280
Yeah. Like, I had noticed that if I had my back to the direction where I wanted to jump, I wouldn't jump as well,

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:53.860
unless I was just imagining this, than if I was facing the direction I wanted to jump.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:58.640
Like, if I was facing right, and I wanted to jump left, and you jump and kind of try and drift left,

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:01.600
it works. It doesn't work as well as if you had already been facing it.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.780
Yeah, no. Yeah, absolutely.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:08.240
I noticed that in general, the horizontal aspect of the jump was terrible.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.980
Like, the verticality of it was fine.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.720
It was like, you know, I jump, and he jumps fast.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.160
I don't know why you move so slowly to the left and right when you move so quickly up and down.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:21.040
And you have to graze the platform that you want to land on to land on it.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.800
Like, there are times where you feel like you're about to, like, land it,

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:27.720
and then you kind of just, like, fall through and go back down.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.240
Right. You definitely clip through the corners of the platforms.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.340
Well, you know, actual mountain climbing is a lot like that.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:40.080
You know, I can't draw too many parallels between actual mountain climbing in this game,

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.500
because I don't know.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.600
I don't know. Like, would you ever?

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:48.840
Well, when you're actually climbing a mountain, the polar bears don't wear Speedos.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:49.980
That's true. Yeah.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.080
Oh, that's interesting. So that was their creative license.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.320
That was a very informative answer.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.600
Also, they don't live on mountains.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.380
So there are no polar bears.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.360
But since we're talking about the difficulty spike, did anybody, like,

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:06.400
did anybody feel about, like, enemies not really, like, meaning that much?

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.980
The enemies really bugged me, just because I feel like at some points I could jump through them,

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:16.900
and it would kill the enemies by jumping from underneath, like, the birds that would fly by.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.060
Oh, being able to hit them with your hammer.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.840
There's a little delay between.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.780
Yeah, if you jump up at them, it's like you're smashing the bricks.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.700
So if you hit them, you hit them with your hammer.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:35.040
Yeah. I didn't realize until, honestly, way well into my playing of this game that you can hit B to just smash your hammer.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.380
I was ignoring one of the four buttons on the controller.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.260
That's why you got to read the manual.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.320
Yeah, Joe, I don't know how you could miss that.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.900
That's, like, a pretty important, like, how were you taking out the enemies?

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.540
I was jumping up to them.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:47.960
I thought I could only jump up.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:52.480
I don't know. I mean, I don't know why I never thought to try pressing B, one of the two buttons.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.380
You made it into, like, a stealth game.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.880
Right. But it didn't make it that much easier.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.640
You know, I never really felt like I needed to kill something that was on the same platform as me.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.940
I always wanted to kill those that were above me so I could get to them.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.240
Okay, so let's jump in.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.500
We talked about the mountains a little bit.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.600
Let's talk about that bonus game, though, where all of a sudden the different vegetable of the week shows up,

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.540
and you just kind of have to collect them as fast as you can.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.940
Anybody got any thoughts on this besides the fact that music is pretty awesome?

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.160
It was pretty difficult.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:22.100
It was pretty difficult to complete a bonus round, at least for me.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.100
And I kept getting tempted by the vegetables.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.460
I don't think I did one bonus round.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:33.880
The ice tripped me up because there's, in the first levels anyway, I don't know about later on because I didn't make it that far,

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:38.460
but there's no ice in it, like any of the first, on, like, the regular part of the stage.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:43.040
Right. And then you get to the top part, and it's all these little small platforms with ice,

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.720
and you're not used to this friction, and the jump is bad.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.200
And so you just, I fell off, I think, after my second jump every single time.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:56.140
Yeah, and it's very cool that they were able to program that, like ice, you know, and, like, being slippery and stuff like that.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.540
I actually wasn't expecting that.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.240
But Sean was my witness.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.100
I did do a bonus game round.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:04.440
I did touch the condor at the end, which I guess is the point.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.480
What happened to the eggplant is beyond us.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.760
I guess he dropped them all.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.080
If you were competing against someone in, like, a race to get through it, if you beat the bonus stage,

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.020
if you're beating the bonus stage and the other person is not, you're probably going to win

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.440
because I think it's, like, the easiest way to get points.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:22.260
Yeah, it is the easiest way to get points, but there's also, there's a lot of points for,

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:26.640
there's a lot of points for the vegetables, too, as you keep going through the levels.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:32.660
Pumpkins was worth, like, I think, like 1,000 on Mountain 7 or something like that.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:33.860
Sean, you had something to say?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.020
I completely forgot.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:39.400
Okay, great. Joe, you robbed him of a thought there.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.300
Well, that's good. I don't want any free thinkers in this podcast.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.660
Absolutely. But, no, can we talk about that music for a second?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.660
I mean, I thought it was pretty good.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.160
I thought that was some of the best NES music we've heard so far.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:56.420
I love, too, when you do complete the bonus stage, since it doesn't seem like a lot of you guys were able to hear it.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.520
It's like, I mean, I'll just play it right now.

